      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got it. So for inner triangulation, descriptive names would look like:\n\n1) stencil curves and breadcrumb triangles\n2) draw or stencil inner triangulation\n3) draw curve convex hulls and breadcrumb triangles\n\nFor middle out triangulation:\n\n1) stencil curves\n2) stencil middle-out inner fan\n3) draw path bounding box\n\nFor wedges:\n\n1) stencil wedges\n2) draw path bounding box\n\nFor convex:\n\n1) draw wedges\n\n\nWhat if we just reserve a range of indices, and each algorithm can define its own internal names for these indices?",
